    {
      "id": "create-and-edit-a-path",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Create and edit a path"
        },
        {
          "type": "tabs",
          "tabs": [
            {
              "label": "Edit vertices",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "example",
                  "example": "labs/pg-path-vertices"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "example",
          "example": "labs/pg-pathscene"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Use setVertices or the dimension setter rather than mutating a cached vertex list without notifying geometry. Path.getPointAtT, tangent, normal, frame and length helpers let you place labels or guide motion along the same geometry. Some length/readback operations require attachment to a scene and a GPU device."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "analytical-fast-and-auto",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Analytical, fast and auto"
        },
        {
          "type": "tabs",
          "tabs": [
            {
              "label": "Analytical",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "example",
                  "example": "labs/pg-pipeline-analytical"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "Fast",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "example",
                  "example": "labs/pg-pipeline-fast"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "Auto",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "example",
                  "example": "labs/pg-pipeline-auto"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Analytical is the Path default: curves are decoded into quadratic contours and rendered using specialized stencil and distance-field stages. Fast mode flattens and triangulates geometry for pooled vertex/index buffers. Auto chooses based on effects and overlap requirements. Switching method rebuilds compatible geometry/fragment/renderer components; it is not a cost-free per-frame toggle."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Analytical paths are resolution independent within the curve approximation and shader tolerances. Fast paths use viewport-aware level of detail, so zoom and tolerance affect tessellation and edge quality. Profile representative content rather than assuming one mode is always faster."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fills-contours-and-closure",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Fills, contours and closure"
        },
        {
          "type": "tabs",
          "tabs": [
            {
              "label": "Closure",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "example",
                  "example": "labs/pg-path-closure"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "Contours and holes",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "example",
                  "example": "labs/pg-path-hole"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Closed contours can contain holes and multiple rings. Fill rules, contour orientation and overlap treatment influence the interior. A line-like path should explicitly use Color.NONE for fill and set the intended closure. Fast-mode fill triangulator and stroke extruder are extension points; custom implementations must match the geometry contract."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Exact contracts: [PathGeometry](/api-components-geometry#pathgeometry), [TriangulatedPathGeometry](/api-components-geometry#triangulatedpathgeometry), [PolyGeometry](/api-components-geometry#polygeometry), [Builder](/api-utils#builder), [PathGeometryUtils](/api-utils#pathgeometryutils)."
        }
      ]
